{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 confirmed RCA (before repair):\n\nThe defect is test isolation, not production auth validation. `tests/unit/test_rp04_s4_llm_runtime_heldout.py:41`, `:60`, and `:125` replace the SDK class `anthropic.AsyncAnthropic` with ordinary functions before the lazily loaded `pydantic_ai.providers.anthropic` module is present. On first import, pydantic-ai 1.107.2 captures the patched function and evaluates its runtime `AsyncAnthropic | AsyncAnthropicBedrock | ...` TypeAlias at installed provider lines 34-36, producing `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: function and type` before rebar reaches `anthropic_auth_kwargs` (`src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:107-119`). `sys.modules` explains the order sensitivity.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof on current main 0f7461d243: each of the three function-patched held-out nodes fails in a fresh Python 3.12.13 process at the union; each passes when the provider is pre-imported. Replacing AsyncAnthropic with a class-shaped double in a fresh process reaches the contractually required secret-free `LLMConfigError`, with constructor count 0. The class-preserving/pre-imported controls pass: `test_only_selected_provider_carrier_consumed`, `test_anthropic_api_key_reaches_the_client`, and `test_construction_guard_fails_fast_on_nonzero_sdk_retries`. A meta-path import blocker observed `events=[provider-import]` and no validation event, proving imports currently precede validation, while an unblocked real-SDK run imports the provider and then raises the correct secret-free LLMConfigError. That ordering is a contributing seam but not an independently authorized production defect: the cited contract at the held-out module lines 3-7, the target nodes, `anthropic_model.py:100-105`, and `auth.py:71-78` promises failure before client construction/request, not before dependency import.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. The existing oracle explicitly requires a typed LLMConfigError and secret-free error message; its function-shaped test double prevents the production behavior from being exercised. Minimal repair target: preserve the SDK symbol’s class contract in all three live sibling patches. No production source change is warranted."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787048503162081001,"uuid":"1ac6d047-1431-48ea-ba70-d099d1d6144e"}